-01-04,746\n2020-01-05,524\n2020-01-06,31\n2020-01-07,53\n2020-01-08,33\n2020-01-09,0\n2020-01-10,33\n2020-01-11,0\n2020-01-12,17\n2020-01-13,48\n2020-01-14,90\n2020-01-15,12\n2020-01-16,0\n2020-01-17,0\n2020-01-18,0\n2020-01-19,0\n2020-01-20,0\n2020-01-21,13\n2020-01-22,52\n2020-01-23,12\n2020-01-24,3\n2020-01-25,0\n2020-01-26,12\n2020-01-27,0\n2020-01-28,0\n2020-01-29,0\n2020-01-30,0\n2020-01-31,0\n2020-02-01,31\n2020-02-02,34\n2020-02-03,0\n2020-02-04,0\n2020-02-05,0\n2020-02-06,0\n2020-02-07,0\n2020-02-08,0\n2020-02-09,0\n2020-02-10,0\n2020-02-11,0\n2020-02-12,0\n2020-02-13,0\n2020-02-14,0\n2020-02-15,0\n2020-02-16,0\n2020-02-17,0\n2020-02-18,0\n2020-02-19,0\n2020-02-20,0\n2020-02-21,0\n2020-02-22,0\n2020-02-23,0\n2020-02-24,0\n2020-02-25,0\n2020-02-26,0\n2020-02-27,0\n2020-02-28,0\n2020-02-29,0\n\"\"\"\ndf = pd.read_csv(io.StringIO(DATA))\n\ndef plot_hotspots(df):\n    \"\"\"MODIS active-fire pixels per day across the study area.\"\"\"\n    df = df.copy()\n    df[\"date\"] = pd.to_datetime(df[\"date\"])\n    df = df.sort_values(\"date\")\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(6.8, 3))\n    ax.bar(df[\"date\"], df[\"hotspots\"], width=1, color=\"#d7191c\")\n    ax.set_ylabel(\"Active-fire pixels per day\")\n    ax.set_title(\"Fire activity, September 2019 to February 2020\", loc=\"left\")\n    fig.autofmt_xdate()\n    return fig\n\nplot_hotspots(df)\nplt.show()\n"
